{"settings":[{"name":"deprecated_using_key_syntax","input_type":"VARCHAR","scope":"GLOBAL","evidence":"> DuckDB 1.5.0 also introduces a new setting to configure the `USING KEY` syntax.
> 
> ```sql
> SET deprecated_using_key_syntax = 'DEFAULT';
> SET deprecated_using_key_syntax = 'UNION_AS_UNION_ALL';
> ```","default_kind":"literal","default_value":"'DEFAULT'","default_evidence":"> Currently, `DEFAULT` enables both syntax styles, i.e., allows both recursive
